**What was built** — a faithful SwiftUI port of `components/feedback/SessionExpiringModal.tsx`:
- **Pure projection core** (`.Adapter`): verbatim port of the web `deriveSessionState` (against an injected clock), `formatCountdown` → `m:ss`, the `open`/visibility predicate, body-phase resolution, and the unsaved-draft sort/cap/overflow.
- **P1/S8 state holder** (`.Model`): binds a `SessionExpiringSource` seam (no HTTP in the view), a 1Hz `tick()` that re-derives so the countdown animates and the dialog auto-hides at expiry, an async `stay()` (web `await refresh()`, "Refreshing…" in-flight), `signOut()`, and `view.opened` telemetry once.
- **Views/States**: every state renders real chrome — hidden (web `null`), loading, empty, error+retry, content (countdown + unsaved-drafts panel + actions), inline-error, stale + offline (chip + banner). Uses shared `TSGlassPanel`/`TSButton`/`TSFadeIn` + P1/S9 tokens; all 8 web i18n keys + native chrome through the P1/S10 facade; VoiceOver labels on every interactive element.
